and *D¹*♭ a Fifth below *A¹*♭ and a major Third below *F*, we obtain the scheme in the central rectangle of the above figures, which is called a *Duodene*, because it consists of *twelve* notes bearing to each other the relation of the twelve notes on the piano, @@F@@
